AB  - In feature selection, the dependency function of rough set theory is commonly used as a feature evaluation function, but it only considers approximated classification information under the decision attribute. This study proposes a feature selection algorithm for partially labeled hybrid data, integrating the ensemble operator of self information, k-nearest neighbors, and Student-t kernel. First, Student-t kernel is introduced to enhance rough set model by defining a novel distance function and similarity measure that better capture the differences across heterogeneous data types. Second, the new ensemble operator of self information is proposed, which integrates the (λ,k)-self information and relative (λ,k)-self information. This operator effectively accounts for uncertainty and classification relevance in feature selection. Finally, comparative experiments and statistical analyses are conducted. Results show that the proposed algorithm significantly outperforms existing algorithms in classification accuracy and feature subset selection. It consistently achieves high accuracy and strong robustness under varying label missing rates. In particular, when the label missing rate is 30%, the algorithm improves the overall average accuracy by 6.02%. Additional analyses, including parameter sensitivity, further confirm that the algorithm provides higher accuracy and more stable performance across different missing label conditions.
