AB  - Sentiment analysis (SA) has emerged as a significant research area due to the surge in user-generated content on online platforms. It is crucial for making informed decisions in fields such as politics, business, and healthcare, as it helps to gauge the opinions, sentiments, and attitudes reflected in textual data. This work comprehensively explores the essential concepts, methodologies, and applications of sentiment analysis, including lexicon-based techniques, traditional machine learning, and advanced transformer-based models and deep learning innovations. The study addresses key challenges that affect Sentiment analysis (SA) systems, including sarcasm detection, management of low-resource languages, and adaptability across different domains. It outlines practical applications such as market forecasting, analysis of customer feedback, public opinion tracking, and mental health assessments. Furthermore, the study provides a thorough analysis of 330 research articles detailing core theories, methodologies, and practical implementations of sentiment analysis. It concludes by proposing future research avenues that encompass the use of multimodal data, enhancement of interpretability, and ethical considerations in sentiment analysis.
