AB  - Condition-based maintenance (CBM) can be defined as a series of steps that lead to a better understanding of a certain equipment. These steps include sensor data collection, data analysis, processing, and prediction methods to ensure the best decision-making action. Through a preliminary investigation, it was observed that the same set of techniques can be efficient in a specific application context, but may not be effective in others. Thus, there is a lack of a more systematized view of which artificial intelligence (AI) and machine learning (ML) techniques have been used by researchers in CBM models, as well as their outcomes. Through a systematic literature review (SLR), this work identified and classified the main AI techniques adopted in CBM models applied to transport systems. It also identified which studies used real-world datasets and which relied on simulated data in their case studies. In addition, the review verified which equipment or systems were monitored in the selected studies. Although the application of AI in CBM for transport systems is a recent research field, it was possible to observe that artificial neural networks (ANN) and support vector machines (SVM) are among the most frequently used AI techniques in this context. Therefore, the application of other AI techniques in CBM remains a vast field for future research and development in transport applications.
