AB  - In complex and unknown three-dimensional scenes, facing the static and ever-changing dynamic obstacles, utilizing the restricted environmental information acquired by sensors poses challenges in real-time path planning for unmanned aerial vehicles (UAVs) to evade obstacles and attain the designated target point. Therefore, this paper proposes a real-time path planning approach grounded in an improved interfered fluid dynamical system (IIFDS) embedded in a fuzzy artificial neural network, aiming to facilitate high-quality real-time path planning. Firstly, a modified gradient-based optimizer (MGBO) with scaled gradient search, adaptively expandable distance, and differential escape operators is proposed to enhance the optimization performance of the algorithm. Then, to tackle the issue of insufficient sample quantity and quality, a method for generating sufficient sample data for artificial neural network training is proposed based on the IIFDS algorithm, which includes MGBO-guided striding rolling time-domain optimization of the path and sample generation based on the nearest obstacles. Subsequently, a fuzzy neural network is proposed in combination with the fuzzy inference system, and the MGBO is used to drive the offline training of the fuzzy neural network weights and biases to effectively improve the prediction ability of the network. Finally, the trained artificial neural network is used to dynamically adjust the parameters of the IIFDS algorithm based on real-time environmental data from sensors, thereby satisfying real-time demands. Experimental results obtained from a range of complex dynamic and static obstacle simulation environments indicate that the proposed algorithm in this paper outperforms compared algorithms in path quality, and has obstacle avoidance capability and real-time performance.
